# Slack automation policy

- Workspace: `day0`.
- Channels: `#revops-asks` (inbound requests), `#revops` (team channel).
- Integration: Slack Web API over HTTPS at `https://slack.com/api/`, bot token in the `Authorization: Bearer` header.

1. The automation registers its app from the team manifest template below, using `apps.manifest.create`. This needs a Slack **app configuration token**, which the messaging administrator issues at approval time. Configuration tokens expire after twelve hours and are never kept in documentation.

```json
{
  "display_information": { "name": "<employee name> (Day0)" },
  "oauth_config": {
    "redirect_urls": ["<Day0 public URL>/api/oauth/slack"],
    "scopes": { "bot": ["chat:write", "channels:read", "users:read.email"] }
  }
}
```

- The manager DM is opened by looking up the manager's email; automations never guess a channel id.

## How an automation gets its own Slack identity

1. Register the app with `apps.manifest.create`. Configuration token (expires in 12h): {{slack_config_token}}
2. The messaging administrator installs the new app from the install link.

